body:
The `refresh()` method returns `false` when there's no FieldWidget for the given field type. According to AG Grid's API, returning `false` means the cell was not refreshed and AG Grid will remove and re-create the cell. For the fallback case (no widget), you should update the textContent and return `true` to avoid unnecessary DOM manipulation.
```suggestion

    // Fallback to text display when no FieldWidget is available
    if (this.eGui) {
      this.eGui.textContent = value != null ? String(value) : '';
      return true;
    }
```
